cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "如果你在報告、論文或改作中使用本軟體，請依下列資訊引用。If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "DTM: Disturbance Torque Monitor for FANUC robot reducers"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: He
    given-names: Domingo
    email: domimgo491@gmail.com
version: 2.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-03"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Domingo-He/dtm-reducer-monitor"
url: "https://github.com/Domingo-He/dtm-reducer-monitor"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  DTM turns the disturbance torque that a FANUC robot controller already computes into a
  reducer health monitor without extra sensors or production stops. It separates friction from
  gravity offset with short diagnostic runs or daily medians of production motions, compares each
  axis with its own baseline, and combines torque with vibration, iron-powder and temperature
  evidence and Weibull component life to recommend grease changes, reducer or gearbox replacement
  and servo-motor inspection. Beta: thresholds still need field validation.
keywords:
  - predictive maintenance
  - condition monitoring
  - industrial robot
  - FANUC
  - RV reducer
  - disturbance torque
  - iron powder
  - Weibull
